extraction_notes: "WB9 printed 26-28 (cache p026-p028; p027 is a full-page illustration with no text). || XP: the Men-Rall / Nazcan Line Maker ladder, printed 192, lower bounds read off a render, stored as given. || GROUP: magic - a spell caster by training, in the Classes of the Empire section with no group heading. No sdc_base or mdc_base printed; men_of_arms: false (a mage, not a man of arms). || MAGIC: drawings are the 25 production Nazca: rows (tradition nazca, level 0). Because the Secret drawings are also level 0 they cannot be held back by a level gate, so every pick is a NAMED LIST: common (the 19 common drawings plus the six invocations) for the eight starting picks and the two per level at 2-5, adept (adds the six Secret drawings) from level 6. The book''s further condition - a Secret drawing only as a reward for service - is a note on those grants, not enforced. spell_traditions_allowed [nazca] is stated so the class''s own tradition is named; every pick is list-bound, so it widens nothing. The six ordinary spells of printed 28 (''in addition to, or instead of, the new line drawing rituals; each spell counts as one ritual'') are in both lists, including the starting picks - ''new'' could be read as level-ups only; recorded here. The book''s ''Summon Entity'' is stored as the catalog''s Summon and Control Entity (level 12), the Rifts invocation of that name; Summon Entities (level 0) was judged a different spell. Diabolist wards are prose (G.M. access). || The line-drawing roll at levels 1-3 and visualization from level 4 are ability text and level_progression. || BONUSES: +1 vs psionics and +4 vs horror factor stored; +1 save vs magic at 3, 6, 9, 11 and 14 as at_level spell_magic; +1 spell strength at 3, 7, 10 and 13 is level_progression only, not stored as a bonus. || P.P.E. 2D4x10 + P.E., +3D6 per level, stored as printed. || SKILLS: Language: Quechua 98 flat (native tongue); two languages +15 as two Language: Other picks; Basic Math 45+20; Art: Line Drawing 35+30; Astronomy 25+15; Demon and Monster Lore is Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+10. The book grants no Hand to Hand: Basic costs one other skill, Expert two, Martial Arts or Assassin (evil) three - the hand_to_hand block prices all four. Related 9, of which two must be Technical (minimums), plus one at 3, 6, 8, 11 and 13. Communications is Basic Radio only (Radio: Basic); Medical is First Aid OR Holistic Medicine, stored as an only of both; Rogue is Prowl only (the catalog files Prowl under Physical, which the class grants). Secondary 6 with the same limits, no bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: feathered headgear has no catalog row and is not stubbed; the camp knife is the catalog knife; the energy weapon and drawing implements are choices from catalog sets; the Jar of Power is the catalog energy-jar row (4D6 stored P.P.E., single use, in its note). 1D6 E-clips rolled. || Cybernetics: none, a restriction. || WARNING: class-check reports ppe_base and starting_money as fields a racial class would discard - the ordinary O.C.C. case; the book does not say the character stops being its race, so no supersedes_race."
