## Lore

The Line Makers descend from the Nazca, a people of great magic who mostly
died or fled Earth when Atlantis fell. The exiles wandered the Megaverse,
some warring for centuries against the surviving Atlanteans, most settling in
pocket dimensions from which they watched their homeland. When the Coming of
the Rifts brought magic back, the great makers opened Rifts of their own and
led ten thousand line makers, with their servants and Rune Warrior guards,
home to the Nazca plateau. They have trained new generations there for three
centuries, and the plateau is now part of the Inca Empire of the Sun.

A Line Maker does not recite spells. He channels will and psychic energy
through precise symbols and patterns, drawn on paper, in the dirt or, with
experience, traced in the air; the precision of the ritual is what makes the
symbol real, and a pattern made permanent can be used again and again.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nazca-line-maker');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nazca-line-maker';

